  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude, slice items[144:150]). biobricks-okg integrates ~10 upstream bricks via RML. The repo LICENSE (MIT) applies only to the mapping code. The aggregated DATA is governed by its most restrictive constituent: CTD (Comparative Toxicogenomics Database) explicitly prohibits commercial reproduction/use without prior written permission and a separate commercial license, and ChEMBL is CC BY-SA 3.0 (share-alike). Therefore the combined graph is classed restricted with commercial use prohibited. HUMAN REVIEW: confirm CTD (ctdbase) data is materially present in the shipped graph; if a CTD-free build were produced, the governing class would relax to share-alike (ChEMBL CC BY-SA) rather than restricted. Verify licenses of the other constituents (bindingdb CC BY, uniprot CC BY 4.0, tox21/toxcast/ice US-gov, hgnc, toxrefdb, mesh).",
